So far this game:

My Priest's first two pets (Cujo and Ceiling Cat) died quickly, but
Cujo II turned into a pit fiend the first time I pushed him onto a
polymorph trap.  The rechristened "Pitunia" has been making short work
of the numerous shopkeepers generated in the game (excepting only
Izchak).  "Would I mind leaving my pick-axe outside?  Hmm.  Let me
whistle my pet over and see what he thinks."

I found two magic lamps in the Mines, giving me GDSM and a blessed
spellbook of identify.

The gate to Ludios was in the first, and so far only, vault I broke
into.

Polypiling the huge pile of weapons and armor in the doorway to the
treasure zoo yielded a T-shirt and an oilskin cloak, neither of which
I had yet seen.

During a polypile session in the vault after I returned from Ludios,
some random piece of junk armor turned into a +4 pair of low boots.  I
also scored a magic marker and +2 ring of increase damage, which goes
well with my +6 flail.

When the vault guard showed up and picked a fight, he dropped a +5
pair of leather gloves when he died.

The only question is:  How badly is the RNG going to screw me over
later in the game?

It's already mocked me a little bit: smoky potions are potions of
healing in this game, and two shopkeepers have summoned djinns when
they quaffed their potions during Pitunia's assaults.  Also, I got
freakin' Sting as my first sacrifice gift.


